+
+## Memory-quality evaluation ledger
+
+Recurring Honcho self-improvement jobs can use `hermes honcho eval` to keep
+longitudinal, content-safe state instead of judging each run in isolation:
+
+```bash
+hermes honcho eval init
+hermes honcho eval native-probes --probe --record --note "hourly loop"
+hermes honcho eval probe --input aggregate-probes.json --record --note "hourly loop"
+hermes honcho eval report
+hermes honcho eval guidance
+```
+
+`eval native-probes` is the preferred hourly source for native Honcho north-star
+evidence. It reads the active profile's Honcho peer card, session context, and a
+small fixed query set in-process, but prints/records only fixed labels and safe
+counts. Use `--probe` to see the sanitized eval-probe payload or `--record` to
+record it directly. It is equivalent to feeding its JSON into `eval probe`, not
+to bypassing the content-safe runner.
+
+`eval probe` is the hourly-safe probe runner for the fixed quality labels
+`recall_usefulness`, `freshness`, `noise`, and `regression` plus operational
+labels `dream_success`, `representation_freshness`, and `budget_efficiency`.
+Feed it a JSON object containing only aggregate counts, ages, rates, booleans,
+and deterministic IDs/labels. The hourly memory-quality contract has two safe
+input shapes:
+
+1. Pre-counted aggregates, for example:
+
+```json
+{
+  "aggregates": {
+    "recall_attempts": 10,
+    "useful_recall_count": 8,
+    "recall_error_count": 1,
+    "fact_count": 20,
+    "recent_fact_count": 16,
+    "stale_fact_count": 2,
+    "max_age_hours": 24,
+    "retrieved_item_count": 30,
+    "irrelevant_item_count": 3,
+    "duplicate_item_count": 2,
+    "regression_checks_total": 5,
+    "regression_checks_failed": 1,
+    "probe_window_label": "hourly-light"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+2. Fixed labeled probe outcomes derived from native Honcho tool results. The
+   hourly loop may call `honcho_profile`, `honcho_context`, and `honcho_search`,
+   but it must reduce their output immediately to sanitized labels such as
+   `query_label`, `probe_label`, `recall_label`, `freshness_label`,
+   `noise_label`, and `regression_label`. The probe runner converts those labels
+   to counts before recording, and never persists retrieved excerpts or peer-card
+   text:
+
+```json
+{
+  "aggregates": {
+    "probe_window_label": "hourly-light",
+    "native_honcho_probe_results": [
+      {
+        "query_label": "talon_identity",
+        "recall_label": "useful",
+        "freshness_label": "fresh",
+        "noise_label": "clean",
+        "regression_label": "pass"
+      },
+      {
+        "query_label": "stale_request_policy",
+        "recall_label": "irrelevant",
+        "freshness_label": "stale",
+        "noise_label": "stale",
+        "regression_label": "fail"
+      }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Labeled probe rows are accepted only when every field name is in the fixed
+contract and every value matches the safe label alphabet `[a-zA-Z0-9_.:/@+-]`.
+Rows containing raw content fields, free-form text, spaces, excerpts, peer-card
+text, prompt/response bodies, secrets, or PII are ignored instead of recorded.
+
+If enough aggregate evidence is present, `eval probe` emits 0..1 scores for the
+labels it can score and, with `--record`, writes only those scores plus safe
+aggregate metadata to the ledger. If quality evidence is missing but operational
+evidence is present, the quality probes are omitted while the operational probes
+still score; this is measurement insufficiency for the omitted labels, not a
+zero-score memory-quality regression. If evidence is missing, the runner records
+omitted probe IDs with machine-safe reasons such as `insufficient_recall_counts`
+instead of guessing.
+
+The hourly operational aggregate contract accepts these content-safe field names
+(aliases may be added as the cron script evolves):
+
+- `dream_success`: `honcho_health_ok`/`health_ok`, `cnpg_query_ok`,
+  `k8s_rollouts_ok`, `hermes_honcho_status_rc`/`honcho_status_rc`,
+  `dream_observation_mode_label=passive`, `dream_schedule_attempted=0`,
+  `dream_schedule_http_status`/`scheduled_joy_talon_dream_http`,
+  `dream_processed`, `queue_error_2h`, `pending_dream_rows`,
+  `deriver_15m_dream_start_markers`/`deriver_2h_dream_start_markers`,
+  `dream_completion_markers`, `deriver_2h_completion_with_errors_count`,
+  `incomplete`/`deriver_2h_incomplete_count`, and
+  `tracebacks`/`deriver_2h_traceback_count`. For passive hourly loops, no
+  active/pending dream is healthy when service and queue evidence are clean;
+  `schedule_dream` status fields are optional legacy evidence, not required.
+- `representation_freshness`: `card_context_readable`/
+  `native_card_context_readable`, `hermes_honcho_status_rc`/
+  `honcho_status_rc`, `queue_error_2h`, and `pending_representation_rows`. A
+  backlog is scored as pressure; it is not treated as missing evidence.
+- `budget_efficiency`: `limiter_15m_503`, `limiter_90m_503`,
+  `limiter_2h_503_count`, `limiter_15m_400`, `limiter_90m_400`,
+  `limiter_2h_400_count`, `limiter_15m_timeout`, `limiter_90m_timeout`,
+  `limiter_2h_timeout_count`, `limiter_15m_prompt_tokens_p95`,
+  `limiter_2h_prompt_tokens_p95`, `limiter_15m_completion_tokens_p95`,
+  `limiter_2h_completion_tokens_p95`, `finish_length`,
+  `deriver_2h_finish_length_count`, `limiter_90m_finish_length`, and
+  `limiter_2h_finish_length_count`.
+
+The default ledger lives under the active profile at
+`state/honcho/memory_quality_ledger.json`. It stores only numeric probe scores,
+aggregate counts, deterministic labels, short sanitized notes, baselines,
+interventions, and deltas. Do not store raw message excerpts, peer-card text,
+retrieved Honcho excerpts, secrets, prompt bodies, or full API responses in the
+input JSON, ledger, logs, Agent Requests, or cron reports. The built-in probe
+suite tracks recall usefulness, freshness, noise, regression, dream success,
+representation freshness, and budget efficiency; cron jobs should compare the
+current score to both the prior run and the current baseline before filing or
+steering Agent Requests.
 
